; @adobe-scoped packages come from Adobe's internal Artifactory, not public npm.
; Without this line, `npm install @adobe/annotations-core` 404s against
; registry.npmjs.org, where the package does not (and should not) exist.
;
; Everything else — react, quill, @react-spectrum/s2, esbuild — stays on the
; public registry, so the default is deliberately left alone.
;
; No credentials here: this file is committed. The auth token for this registry
; path lives in your personal ~/.npmrc. If `npm install` returns 401/404 for an
; @adobe package, mint one from artifactory.corp.adobe.com (Set Me Up → npm)
; and add it to ~/.npmrc as:
;   //artifactory.corp.adobe.com/artifactory/api/npm/npm-adobe-release/:_authToken=<token>
@adobe:registry=https://artifactory.corp.adobe.com/artifactory/api/npm/npm-adobe-release/
